      "raw": "Hyrax, Lorax, and Average-Elevationrax.\n\nA pine marten's not a rodent!  Mustelids are not rodentia!\n\nMayor Maeknaught\n\nOoof, the Department of Exo-Earth Integration\n..that didn't age well....\n\nWager Master dies a lot...especially on-stage! *badum-tish!*\n\nInteresting that C&A made a character specifically Ukrainian a full year before the war with Russia broke out.\n\nName: Sky-Scraper\nAlias: Portja Kir-Pro\nSpecies: Thorathian (powered)\nNationality: Earthling\n\nWhat villain should go to DokThorath? Send me Fright Train, he can help them build a commuter train system, and the trains will all just run on time by default!\n\n\"Propagandists Adam and Christopher\" :joy: :joy: :joy: :joy:\n\nIf Aata-Haka had a good enough reason to get back to universe 1, I think he could find a reality outside the sandwich bag which Hul had devoured through an alternate Xxtz'hulissh, get alt-Xxtz to swallow him, travel across whatever unknowable alien landscape exists within Hul, and tear his way out again through the maw of Xxtz-1.  The problem is that while Haka's life is guaranteed against destruction by Arataki's continued existence, his sanity is not.  Even if the purpose of reaching his original home remained intact, the Haka that returned from Hul would not be the person we know and love.\n\nZhu Long was not from Atlantis.  But perhaps he was the direct student of someone who was, or better yet stole the power of one.",
